PXL
----

Minimal 2D graphics library in C99.

Features:
  - 2D primitives: line, rect, circle, triangle (outline + filled)
  - Canvas with scissor clipping, translation offset, color, clear, blit
  - Test outputting using either built-in 8x8 ascii font or monospace or
    proportional bitmask font
  - Backends: SDL2, X11
  - Keyboard/mouse input

Build:
  make          # lib
  make lint     # run lint
  make test     # run tests
  make demo     # demos
  make clean    # cleaning

  Configuration posible using config.mk.
  'Release mode' (remove "asserts") via PXL_BUILD_MODE=release.
  Backend selection via PXL_BACKEND=sdl or PXL_BACKEND=x11 (default).

  Main configuration is defined in Makefile.inc. Override in config.mk or via
  environment variables.

Quick start:
    pxl_input_t in = {0};
    pxl_backend_init("Title", 800, 600, 0);
    while (pxl_input_state(&in, PXL_KEYB_ESCAPE) == 0 &&
           pxl_input_state(&in, PXL_WM_QUIT) == 0) {
        pxl_backend_poll_events(&in);

        pxl_buf_t pb;
        if (pxl_backend_begin_frame(&pb) == PXL_SUCCESS) {
            pxl_canvas_t cnv;
            pxl_canvas_init(&cnv, &pb);
            /* drawing: pxl_draw_*(), pxl_fill_*(), pxl_canvas_clear() */
            pxl_backend_end_frame();
        }
    }
    pxl_backend_deinit();

Demos:
  - demo_pong.c       - Pong game
  - demo_gas.c        - Boltzmann gas simulation
  - demo_typewriter.c - Text typing animation
  - demo_fountain.c   - Particle fountain with tileset/sprite


Architecture:
  Core:
    err.h          - Error codes
    buf.h          - uint32_t pixel buffer with stride alignment
    input.h        - Input state handling (keyboard, mouse, window events)
    backend.h      - Backend interface. All backends use ARGB8888 pixel format
                     (A:24-31, R:16-23, G:8-15, B:0-7).

  Backend:
    input.h       - Input state handling (keyboard, mouse, window events)
    backend.h     - Backend interface. All backends MUST use ARGB8888 pixel format
                    (A:24-31, R:16-23, G:8-15, B:0-7). Supports both little-endian and
                    big-endian architectures via color.h helpers (pxl_argb, pxl_a, etc.).
                    Only one window is supported at the moment.
    backend_sdl.c - SDL2 backend (do not activate VSYNC)
    backend_x11.c - X11 backend

  Gfx:
    bitmask.h      - 1-bit per pixel mask for stencil/clip operations
    canvas.h       - Drawing surface with color, scissor, translation offset, clear, blit
    geom.h         - Geometry primitives (rect, span, point) and clipping
    shape.h/c      - 2D primitives (line, rect, circle, triangle, outline + filled)
    blit.h/c       - Pixel operations (blit, bitmask drawing)
    text_basic.h/c - ASCII text rendering with built-in 8x8 font (char, string, bounds)
    color.h        - ARGB8888 color creation and component extraction

  Framework:
    stepper.h      - Time-stepped physics loop helper (fixed timestep, interpolation)
    text.h/text.c  - Text rendering with mono or proportional LSB bitmask font
    tileset.h/c    - Tile rendering: grid atlas (tileset) + animation frames (sprite)

  Note: pxl.h includes all public headers above. Users may include individual headers if preferred.

Tools:
  - bdf2pxl - Convert BDF font files to pxl_font_t C header
    Example: bdf2pxl -n my_font -r U+0020-U+007F DejaVuSans.bdf > my_font.h

Testing:
  Framework: test.h (minimalist assert-based testing)
  Run tests: make test or sh test.sh to go through all available backends.

